****Custom properties with @Input()

@Input() allows a parent component to supply a value to a child component.

Think of the child as a reusable machine. The parent supplies the data, and the child uses it to produce the correct UI.

******Is the child component inside the parent component?
Yes, visually and structurally, but not literally inside the parent's TypeScript class. This distinction is important.